ble {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "31 July –  1 August 1992"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/668"} "Estadio Olímpico de Montjuïc, Barcelona"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/63952"} "81 from 66 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The last five major international championships in the 100 had all been won by " [:a {:href "/athletes/78692"} "Carl Lewis"] " – the 1984 and 1988 Olympic Games, and the 1983, 1987, and 1991 World Champinoships. But in both 1990 and 1991, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78178"} "Leroy Burrell"] " (USA) was ranked as #1 in the world by " [:em {} "Track &amp; Field News"] ". In 1990 he was chased by Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/68957"} "Linford Christie"] ", who won both the Commonwealth Games and the European Championships. Lewis, hampered by a viral infection at the Trials, only made the US team in the long jump. Burrell and " [:a {:href "/athletes/78798"} "Dennis Mitchell"] " both qualified for the 100. Burrell and Christie looked on top form in the prelims, with Burrell defeating Christie 9.97 to 10.00 in the semis into a headwind. But in the final, after two false starts, Burrell started very slowly and was never in the race. Christie won fairly comfortably with a charge in the last 50 metres. Namibia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/73682"} "Frank Fredericks"] " was second, and Mitchell won the bronze medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "695"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/68957"} "Linford Christie"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:cla